<title>USA: Borders says C-SPAN's Lamb resigns as dir.</title>
<headline>Borders says C-SPAN's Lamb resigns as dir.</headline>
<dateline>ANN ARBOR, Mich. 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borders Group Inc said that Brian Lamb, the chairman and chief executive of C-SPAN, has resigned as a director of the company.</p>
<p>Lamb said that he decided he should step down from the post because C-SPAN's recent expansion of its book-related programs &quot;has led me to conclude that it is no longer appropriate for me to serve as a director of any bookseller.&quot;</p>
<p>(-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610)</p>
</text>
